-- The lifecycle Service: what a reset does, as a Script (ADR 0024). A
-- System or timer decides when a place is due; mua then sends this
-- Service `reset place`, and afterwards tells the place's own Scripts.
--
-- A reset puts back every thing whose home is the place and that has
-- wandered, unless a Character is carrying it. It returns how many moved.

-- whether a Character holds this, directly or inside something they carry
function carried thing, seen
  if the location of thing is nothing then
    return false
  end if
  ask world to resolve the in of the location of thing into holder
  if holder is nothing or holder is in seen then
    return false
  end if
  if the player of holder is not nothing then
    return true
  end if
  return carried(holder, [...seen, thing])
end carried

on reset place
  put 0 into moved
  ask mua to homed place into homed
  repeat for each thing in homed
    put nothing into here
    if the location of thing is not nothing then
      ask world to resolve the in of the location of thing into here
    end if
    if here is not place and not carried(thing, []) then
      moveTo thing, place
      put moved + 1 into moved
    end if
  end repeat
  return moved
end reset
